# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the linux-tsan preset.
#
# LLVM registers each statistic lazily, the first time it is used, behind a
# lock and an atomic "registered" flag. libLLVM is not built with TSan, so the
# flag's atomic accesses are invisible and two parser threads registering at
# once look like a race on the statistic. Both stacks are entirely inside
# libLLVM; Tezcatl's code appears only as the creator of the thread. Scoped to
# that one function, so a race in Tezcatl's own state is still reported.
race:llvm::TrackingStatistic::RegisterStatistic
